<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Mod id="8c3f1a52-6d7e-4b19-9a40-52e0c7d1b6a3" version="101">
	<Properties>
		<Name>Ability Draft</Name>
		<Teaser>Draft the leader, the civilization and each unique item separately in the multiplayer lobby</Teaser>
		<Description>Ability Draft for Gathering Storm (Gathering Storm rules only). In the multiplayer lobby (LAN or internet) every player picks a leader, a civilization, a unique district, building, improvement and unit, each from its own menu; any menu can be a secret random pick. The leader brings only his ability, the civilization only its ability, and the picked unique items become the player's own. An ability that names a district or building works with every district or building of that kind (a unique one or the one it replaces). Supports up to 12 players. Optional game setting: items named in an ability stay with that ability. With Better Balanced Starts (BBS), start positions follow the draft: sea-related picks pull the start to the coast. Single player and hot seat are not supported. Not compatible with Multiplayer Helper.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Source code and bug reports: github.com/maksdk87/Ability-Draft-Civilization-VI (Discussions, "Ability Draft Bugs").[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Thanks to: the Better Balanced Game team (BBG, github.com/CivilizationVIBetterBalancedGame) and the BBG Expanded authors; 57F@n and D. / Jack The Narrator (Better Balanced Starts); BaNiPouZ and Talasta (Better Balanced Map); Cisco and D. / Jack The Narrator (Multiplayer Helper); Lee "LeeS" Shipp (Civilization 6 Modding Guide); the editors of the Civilization Wiki (Fandom); Firaxis Games, whose own lobby scripts this lobby is built on.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Made with the help of Claude Opus 5.5 by Anthropic (model claude-opus-5-5), effort: Extra.</Description>
		<Version>0.1.1</Version>
		<Authors>enjoymyragga (github.com/maksdk87)</Authors>
		<SupportsSinglePlayer>0</SupportsSinglePlayer>
		<SupportsMultiplayer>1</SupportsMultiplayer>
		<SupportsHotSeat>0</SupportsHotSeat>
		<AffectsSavedGames>1</AffectsSavedGames>
		<CompatibleVersions>2.0</CompatibleVersions>
	</Properties>
	<Dependencies>
		<Mod id="4873eb62-8ccc-4574-b784-dda455e74e68" title="Expansion: Gathering Storm" />
	</Dependencies>
